(1296228, 166713, 34192, '<td valign="top">Where''s the angel?  Too bad there are no tacks in this image. ;)  Excellent job.  I want to know how you did it.  I think the tone and composition are excellent.  Not everything has to abide by the rule of thirds!  DOV and POV excellent.  10 because this is a great image to create in 24 hours.</td>', 'Where''s the angel?  Too bad there are no tacks in this image. ;)  Excellent job.  I want to know how you did it.  I think the tone and composition are excellent.  Not everything has to abide by the rule of thirds!  DOV and POV excellent.  10 because this is a great image to create in 24 hours.', '2005-04-16 12:35:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296229, 167029, 24890, '<td valign="top">This is great! 9 for the picture... 10 because it is funny!</td>', 'This is great! 9 for the picture... 10 because it is funny!', '2005-04-16 12:36:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296230, 166739, 27482, '<td valign="top">Sorry if I seem harsh but I can´t give this anything but a 2 and the only reason I am not giving it a 1 is that it seems on topic as I am guessing those are tacks that are in the floorboards.  The image is horribly out of focus, totally uninteresting and poorly framed and to me it seems like this shot is made by accident as if the camera shot this itself as you dropped it on the floor.  Again, sorry if I seem harsh but this is a very bad image.  My tips on how to improve for next time is to have the main subject (in this case the tacks in front) in focus, try to light it more evenly next time.  This can be done by using a tripod and take the picture with a slower shutterspeed to get the dark parts in the picture brighter and turn off the flash to make the front of the floorboards darker and lit the same way as the rest of the floorboards.  Lastly, find a more interesting subject, ask yourself, is this something you would proudly hang up on a wall?  My guess is no and if that is the case, you need to put in a better effort.  Anyway, I have a gut feeling you can do better, now go out and prove me right and enter a better image in the next challenge.<br/> <br/>Again, apologize if I seem harsh but I mean this in the best way possible, feel free to PM if I offended you in any way.</td>', 'Sorry if I seem harsh but I can´t give this anything but a 2 and the only reason I am not giving it a 1 is that it seems on topic as I am guessing those are tacks that are in the floorboards.  The image is horribly out of focus, totally uninteresting and poorly framed and to me it seems like this shot is made by accident as if the camera shot this itself as you dropped it on the floor.  Again, sorry if I seem harsh but this is a very bad image.  My tips on how to improve for next time is to have the main subject (in this case the tacks in front) in focus, try to light it more evenly next time.  This can be done by using a tripod and take the picture with a slower shutterspeed to get the dark parts in the picture brighter and turn off the flash to make the front of the floorboards darker and lit the same way as the rest of the floorboards.  Lastly, find a more interesting subject, ask yourself, is this something you would proudly hang up on a wall?  My guess is no and if that is the case, you need to put in a better effort.  Anyway, I have a gut feeling you can do better, now go out and prove me right and enter a better image in the next challenge. Again, apologize if I seem harsh but I mean this in the best way possible, feel free to PM if I offended you in any way.', '2005-04-16 12:36:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296233, 166944, 34192, '<td valign="top">A very unusual tack. Alas, there is only 1.  This challenge called for TACKS. ;)  The lighting here is a little harsh and the image seems oversharpened a bit. 6 for now, may bump later.</td>', 'A very unusual tack. Alas, there is only 1.  This challenge called for TACKS. ;)  The lighting here is a little harsh and the image seems oversharpened a bit. 6 for now, may bump later.', '2005-04-16 12:38:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296234, 167026, 24890, '<td valign="top">Ha Ha! Thanks for the laugh! 10</td>', 'Ha Ha! Thanks for the laugh! 10', '2005-04-16 12:38:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296239, 166746, 1, '<td valign="top">The relections are cool, but there''s nothing in the image that really screams for my attention...  The centered tack almost does, but I think the photo would''ve benefited from 1 tack being silver or a just different color.</td>', 'The relections are cool, but there''s nothing in the image that really screams for my attention...  The centered tack almost does, but I think the photo would''ve benefited from 1 tack being silver or a just different color.', '2005-04-16 12:39:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296241, 167057, 34192, '<td valign="top">Wow!  This is so cool!  The only problem I see is that there are no tacks in this image. ;)  Really well done.  Where did you get the giant tacks?  Wish the DOF would have covered the slightly out of focus planetoid.  But the capture of the light ''star'' on the green pin makes up for it.    You''ve managed to capture some depth in the individual tacks - you can see they are rounded rather than flat as in a lot of the other images.  Good work!  10 from me!</td>', 'Wow!  This is so cool!  The only problem I see is that there are no tacks in this image. ;)  Really well done.  Where did you get the giant tacks?  Wish the DOF would have covered the slightly out of focus planetoid.  But the capture of the light ''star'' on the green pin makes up for it.    You''ve managed to capture some depth in the individual tacks - you can see they are rounded rather than flat as in a lot of the other images.  Good work!  10 from me!', '2005-04-16 12:41:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296242, 167057, 1, '<td valign="top">Nice, I''m interested in how you pulled this off.  The lens flare is great, as is the glowing planet that the tacks are sticking into.  The only problem I see is that the background planet is getting a lot of light while the tacks don''t seem to be receiving the same amount.</td>', 'Nice, I''m interested in how you pulled this off.  The lens flare is great, as is the glowing planet that the tacks are sticking into.  The only problem I see is that the background planet is getting a lot of light while the tacks don''t seem to be receiving the same amount.', '2005-04-16 12:42:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296246, 166824, 1, '<td valign="top">This is a nicely composed shot, but I''m not sure that the things on the seat are tacks.</td>', 'This is a nicely composed shot, but I''m not sure that the things on the seat are tacks.', '2005-04-16 12:43:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296247, 166708, 34192, '<td valign="top">Okay, I am not going to mark you down for having a political bobblehead.  That is a personal choice made outside DPC.  And you did use a really tack.  Unfortunately, there is only one and the challenge called for TACKS. ;)  Pretty good capture.  Focus is not the best but the background is not overwhelming.  Composition simple and stright forward. 7 frome me!  good luck!</td>', 'Okay, I am not going to mark you down for having a political bobblehead.  That is a personal choice made outside DPC.  And you did use a really tack.  Unfortunately, there is only one and the challenge called for TACKS. ;)  Pretty good capture.  Focus is not the best but the background is not overwhelming.  Composition simple and stright forward. 7 frome me!  good luck!', '2005-04-16 12:44:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296249, 167019, 24890, '<td valign="top">Should be a ribbon winner.</td>', 'Should be a ribbon winner.', '2005-04-16 12:46:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296250, 166957, 1, '<td valign="top">Good lord this must have taken a looooong time.  The effect is great though!  My only problem is the images in the front ruin your nice pattern.  I would''ve just done a tight crop over the pattern or had the tacks trail off while following the pattern.</td>', 'Good lord this must have taken a looooong time.  The effect is great though!  My only problem is the images in the front ruin your nice pattern.  I would''ve just done a tight crop over the pattern or had the tacks trail off while following the pattern.', '2005-04-16 12:48:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296252, 167019, 1, '<td valign="top">Nice idea!  I think the light may be too harsh on one side though.  A more even (but certainly not equal) distribution of light would''ve benefited this image.</td>', 'Nice idea!  I think the light may be too harsh on one side though.  A more even (but certainly not equal) distribution of light would''ve benefited this image.', '2005-04-16 12:49:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296253, 166962, 34192, '<td valign="top">Finally!  Real tacks! ;)  I think using the grater is a great idea for texture.  I may use that in the future if you don''t mind.  Is that cheating?  I think it might have been better the crop out a little more of the left side but pretty cool the way it is.  Like the lighting.   The focus is a touch soft. 8 for the originality and teaching me a new use for a grater.   Thanks!</td>', 'Finally!  Real tacks! ;)  I think using the grater is a great idea for texture.  I may use that in the future if you don''t mind.  Is that cheating?  I think it might have been better the crop out a little more of the left side but pretty cool the way it is.  Like the lighting.   The focus is a touch soft. 8 for the originality and teaching me a new use for a grater.   Thanks!', '2005-04-16 12:50:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296254, 166798, 1, '<td valign="top">Cool idea, I like the composition a lot.. the colors/light are a little washed out though.</td>', 'Cool idea, I like the composition a lot.. the colors/light are a little washed out though.', '2005-04-16 12:52:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296255, 166901, 34192, '<td valign="top">Simple and to the point - the way I love my tacks.  The reflection is bizarre.  Can''t decide if I like it or not.  The focus is spot on - DOF could have been just a hair larger to get the tip of the tack in focus.  8 from me!</td>', 'Simple and to the point - the way I love my tacks.  The reflection is bizarre.  Can''t decide if I like it or not.  The focus is spot on - DOF could have been just a hair larger to get the tip of the tack in focus.  8 from me!', '2005-04-16 12:52:16.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1296257, 167022, 30315, '<td valign="top">Great concept... :)</td>', 'Great concept... :)', '2005-04-16 12:53:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296260, 167033, 30315, '<td valign="top">I like the idea, but what gets me are the reflections. I''m always a sucker for a curved reflection! Nice!</td>', 'I like the idea, but what gets me are the reflections. I''m always a sucker for a curved reflection! Nice!', '2005-04-16 12:54:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296261, 167037, 34192, '<td valign="top">There are no tacks in this image. ;)  That blob of gum is gross.  I hate scraping it off my shoe.  Couldn''t imagine getting it stuck on my head.   The detail in the stretched part of the gum is excellent.  I think the DOF could have been a little larger to get everything more in focus.  Composition works well. 7 from me.  Good luck!</td>', 'There are no tacks in this image. ;)  That blob of gum is gross.  I hate scraping it off my shoe.  Couldn''t imagine getting it stuck on my head.   The detail in the stretched part of the gum is excellent.  I think the DOF could have been a little larger to get everything more in focus.  Composition works well. 7 from me.  Good luck!', '2005-04-16 12:54:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296262, 166952, 34192, '<td valign="top">Why is he so angry?  At least you got TACKS in here!  I think the background would be better if it was flat rather than textured.  The texture detracts from the important part of the image - the tacks.  Great job finding a smiley face tack!  7 for the creativity.</td>', 'Why is he so angry?  At least you got TACKS in here!  I think the background would be better if it was flat rather than textured.  The texture detracts from the important part of the image - the tacks.  Great job finding a smiley face tack!  7 for the creativity.', '2005-04-16 12:56:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296263, 166959, 22551, '<td valign="top">Not crazy about the shots where people are impaled by the tax but this one is much better than the others.</td>', 'Not crazy about the shots where people are impaled by the tax but this one is much better than the others.', '2005-04-16 12:58:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296264, 166919, 34192, '<td valign="top">Ouch!  I like your foot better than the other one I saw but there are no tacks in this image. ;)  So, did the person scream?  What, they didn''t put their foot down?!  I really like the lighting and think the composition works.  The drapes in the upper right are a little distracting but the focus and POV are excellent.  8 may bump later.</td>', 'Ouch!  I like your foot better than the other one I saw but there are no tacks in this image. ;)  So, did the person scream?  What, they didn''t put their foot down?!  I really like the lighting and think the composition works.  The drapes in the upper right are a little distracting but the focus and POV are excellent.  8 may bump later.', '2005-04-16 12:58:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296266, 167023, 30315, '<td valign="top">Awesome! Very cool shot! My 10!</td>', 'Awesome! Very cool shot! My 10!', '2005-04-16 12:59:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296267, 167022, 22551, '<td valign="top">very clever and nicely executed</td>', 'very clever and nicely executed', '2005-04-16 12:59:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296271, 167004, 34192, '<td valign="top">poor dead turtle.  Where are the tacks? ;)  Interesting image.  Focus is good.  The white tack stands out - maybe a different color would lessen the focus on that particular tack. 7 for now, may bump later.</td>', 'poor dead turtle.  Where are the tacks? ;)  Interesting image.  Focus is good.  The white tack stands out - maybe a different color would lessen the focus on that particular tack. 7 for now, may bump later.', '2005-04-16 13:01:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296272, 166851, 34192, '<td valign="top">pretty.  And they are real tacks!  Good abstract shot.  Would have liked a slightly better focus or DOF but the composition and colors work. 7 from me!</td>', 'pretty.  And they are real tacks!  Good abstract shot.  Would have liked a slightly better focus or DOF but the composition and colors work. 7 from me!', '2005-04-16 13:02:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296275, 167063, 34192, '<td valign="top">Yes.  Way too many - like an invading hoard of ants!  This works for me - the DOF, tones, composition; I like.  POV could have been slightly lower but thats just a nitpick. 8 cause I think you did well.</td>', 'Yes.  Way too many - like an invading hoard of ants!  This works for me - the DOF, tones, composition; I like.  POV could have been slightly lower but thats just a nitpick. 8 cause I think you did well.', '2005-04-16 13:04:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296276, 167058, 8624, '<td valign="top">great lighting. good use of hadows and I like the reflective surfaces</td>', 'great lighting. good use of hadows and I like the reflective surfaces', '2005-04-16 13:04:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296280, 166695, 34192, '<td valign="top">Oh yuck!  Shave those toe knuckles!  The challenge called for TACKS.  There is only one tack in this image. ;)  Macro good - I may be able to find oyu later through a toe print!  Think the tones you used are excellent.  POV and DOF all well done. Gotta give you a 9. May want to buff out that callous there... ;)</td>', 'Oh yuck!  Shave those toe knuckles!  The challenge called for TACKS.  There is only one tack in this image. ;)  Macro good - I may be able to find oyu later through a toe print!  Think the tones you used are excellent.  POV and DOF all well done. Gotta give you a 9. May want to buff out that callous there... ;)', '2005-04-16 13:06:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296282, 167057, 18403, '<td valign="top">Absolutely the best composition in this challenge. Great lighting! 10</td>', 'Absolutely the best composition in this challenge. Great lighting! 10', '2005-04-16 13:08:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296283, 167049, 34192, '<td valign="top">Okay.  These are the ugliest feet in the challenge.  No offense, but they really are!  and you only have 1 tack. ;) 6  for the anticipation of the scream to follow the footstep :)</td>', 'Okay.  These are the ugliest feet in the challenge.  No offense, but they really are!  and you only have 1 tack. ;) 6  for the anticipation of the scream to follow the footstep :)', '2005-04-16 13:08:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296284, 167000, 34192, '<td valign="top">I am so glad I am not your neighbor.  There are no tacks in this image. ;)  Very intriguing.  You''ve made it mysterious and ominous with your use of lighting and  tone.  Definitely set a mood. 7 for the creativity and the image.</td>', 'I am so glad I am not your neighbor.  There are no tacks in this image. ;)  Very intriguing.  You''ve made it mysterious and ominous with your use of lighting and  tone.  Definitely set a mood. 7 for the creativity and the image.', '2005-04-16 13:10:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296299, 166691, 18738, '<td valign="top">looks like a camera strap</td>', 'looks like a camera strap', '2005-04-16 13:16:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296304, 166880, 18738, '<td valign="top">scary picture</td>', 'scary picture', '2005-04-16 13:19:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296309, 166918, 6804, '<td valign="top">My eye went straight to the tack on this!  I sat here for a few min looking at how much there is in this photo and how small and seemingly insignificant the tack is.  This picture says a lot for leadlines and utilization of the rule of thirds.  I''m wondering how many comments you are getting about the tack being too hard to find.  I had no trouble at all.  I find this to be an interesting study.  I wonder if I were looking at this picture without the topic in my head if I would still see the tack as quickly as I did.  The Eye goes 1st to the large dark patch in the upper left and then follows the leadlines and stops on the tack at the rule of 3rds.  Remarkable use of lines and spots to bring such a great amount of attention to such a small area of the picture.  10</td>', 'My eye went straight to the tack on this!  I sat here for a few min looking at how much there is in this photo and how small and seemingly insignificant the tack is.  This picture says a lot for leadlines and utilization of the rule of thirds.  I''m wondering how many comments you are getting about the tack being too hard to find.  I had no trouble at all.  I find this to be an interesting study.  I wonder if I were looking at this picture without the topic in my head if I would still see the tack as quickly as I did.  The Eye goes 1st to the large dark patch in the upper left and then follows the leadlines and stops on the tack at the rule of 3rds.  Remarkable use of lines and spots to bring such a great amount of attention to such a small area of the picture.  10', '2005-04-16 13:20:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296314, 166911, 18738, '<td valign="top">Fantastic, but I found the highlights around the bottom left distracting.</td>', 'Fantastic, but I found the highlights around the bottom left distracting.', '2005-04-16 13:22:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296315, 166987, 36078, '<td valign="top">I love the water drop ripples.  Very classic style picture.</td>', 'I love the water drop ripples.  Very classic style picture.', '2005-04-16 13:23:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296316, 166963, 18738, '<td valign="top">Ah, but the point isn''t clear.</td>', 'Ah, but the point isn''t clear.', '2005-04-16 13:23:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296321, 167006, 18738, '<td valign="top">Stunning. I don''t like the foreground though, blurred foregrounds put me off, but I can see a good argument for that particular composition.</td>', 'Stunning. I don''t like the foreground though, blurred foregrounds put me off, but I can see a good argument for that particular composition.', '2005-04-16 13:26:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1296322, 167054, 18738, '<td valign="top">you lazy child</td>', 'you lazy child', '2005-04-16 13:26:49.000000', NULL, 1),
