(1296391, 166906, 34192, '<td valign="top">Cool!  I was going to do this!  But I was using REAL tacks so the final result was not as good. ;)  I like what you used for a background.  Can''t remember what its called but it provides great texture here.  Competes a little with the tacks,  but the color works beautifully with the orange.  Centered composition - many would say its a no-no.  Forget them - the real rule is that a composition needs to be balanced.  You achieve that with your color choice.  Also, people believe center compositions don''t provide tension.  Again, yours is in the color and texture choices you made.  I like it.  Its hard to make tacks interesting.  9 for your use of color and comp.  Focus and DOF and POV great, BTW.</td>', 'Cool!  I was going to do this!  But I was using REAL tacks so the final result was not as good. ;)  I like what you used for a background.  Can''t remember what its called but it provides great texture here.  Competes a little with the tacks,  but the color works beautifully with the orange.  Centered composition - many would say its a no-no.  Forget them - the real rule is that a composition needs to be balanced.  You achieve that with your color choice.  Also, people believe center compositions don''t provide tension.  Again, yours is in the color and texture choices you made.  I like it.  Its hard to make tacks interesting.  9 for your use of color and comp.  Focus and DOF and POV great, BTW.', '2005-04-16 14:01:54.000000', NULL, 1),
